      "type": "policy",
      "title": "AMD-SUP-2026-02 Amendment 2 to the Supplier Policy",
      "facts": [
        {
          "fact": "AMD-SUP-2026-02 is version 1.0, authored by L. Moreno on 2026-08-14, effective 2026-09-01, owned by the Purchase department, and has status CURRENT.",
          "quote": "AMD-SUP-2026-02 Version 1.0 Effective 2026-09-01 Owner Purchase department, Northbridge Cycles Status CURRENT",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "Field",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "Effective 1 September 2026, Supplier Policy POL-SUP-003 §4.4 is replaced such that a UN 38.3 certificate is accepted only if issued within the last 12 months, and its valid-to date is at least 60 days after the order placement date.",
          "quote": "With effect from 1 September 2026, Supplier Policy POL-SUP-003 §4.4 is replaced by the following: \"A UN 38.3 certificate is accepted only if it was issued within the last 12 months, and its valid-to date is at least 60 days after the date the order is placed.\"",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "1. What changes",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "A certificate meeting the old rule of being issued within 24 months and not expired counts as no certificate for new orders placed from 1 September 2026, whereas orders released before that date are not affected.",
          "quote": "A certificate that meets the old rule (issued within 24 months and not expired) but not the new one counts as no certificate for new orders from 1 September 2026. Orders released before that date are not affected.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "1. What changes",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "The policy change was prompted by a July 2026 incident where a battery pack lot from a supplier with a 22-month-old test report failed Northbridge's incoming abuse test because the cell maker had changed.",
          "quote": "In July 2026 a battery pack lot from a supplier with a 22-month-old test report failed our own incoming abuse test. The cell maker had changed in the meantime.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "2. Why",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "Purchase staff must check the issue date and valid-to date of a lithium-cell part's certificate against the new rule before raising an order.",
          "quote": "Before raising an order for a lithium-cell part, check the certificate's issue date and its valid-to date against the new rule.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "The senior buyer must run the certificate-expiry report per MAN-PUR-72 §22.6 on the first working day of each month with a 90-day window and notify every supplier whose UN 38.3 certificate expires within it.",
          "quote": "The senior buyer runs the certificate-expiry report (MAN-PUR-72 §22.6) on the first working day of each month with 90 days as the window, and writes to every supplier whose UN 38.3 certificate expires inside it.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "All other parts of POL-SUP-003 §4 remain in effect.",
          "quote": "Every other part of POL-SUP-003 §4 stands.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
